{"name":"Just Perfect","hex":"#eaecd3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"just","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Factually right, correct; factual.","Rationally right, correct."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Only, simply, merely.","Introduces a disappointing or surprising outcome that renders futile something previously mentioned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/just"},{"term":"perfect","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fitting its definition precisely.","Having all of its parts in harmony with a common purpose."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The perfect tense, or a form in that tense.","A perfect score; the achievement of finishing a stage or task with no mistakes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect"}],"entries":[{"title":"Just Perfect","blocks":[{"text":"\"Just Perfect\" is a song by the American punk rock band All, released as a single from their 1988 debut album Allroy Sez. Written by drummer Bill Stevenson, \"Just Perfect\" was remixed from the original album version for release as a single. The B-side track \"Wishing Well\", written by singer Dave Smalley, is from the Allroy Sez recording sessions but was not included on the album. Both tracks were later included on the compact disc release of All's following EP, Allroy for Prez (1988)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/All_-_Just_Perfect_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Just_Perfect","wikidata":"Q19893507"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"just":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/En-us-just.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/87/En-us-just.ogg/En-us-just.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"h